The code statements that lead to the bug are:
engine->set_default_submission(engine);
Reason:
When the i915 driver firmware binaries are absent, the function pointer `engine->set_default_submission` is not initialized and remains NULL. During suspend, `intel_engines_reset_default_submission()` unconditionally dereferences this NULL pointer, causing a kernel NULL pointer dereference and crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (engine->set_default_submission)
    engine->set_default_submission(engine);
Reason:
The fix adds a NULL check before dereferencing `engine->set_default_submission`. If the pointer is not set (remains NULL), the call is skipped, preventing the NULL pointer dereference and allowing the system to suspend normally even when firmware binaries are missing.

